  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The HP Reverb G2, as well as possibly any Mixed reality headset, and other non-touch sensor tracked controllers, is having a major issue with the new system. Unless a gesture is being made, the avatar defaults to hand-open. Originally the controllers could only perform gestures via button press, including using (tilting/pressing) the joysticks for the thumb tracking. The new update changes it to the buttons (ABXY) which causes issues since these buttons have functions already including mute, menu, and jump. It also changes it so that while not using any buttons, the tracking defaults to hand open. It was annoying before to perform gestures, but being stuck in hand-open mode requires me to press these buttons to use rest mode. I've attempted turning off all items related to this update, using legacy tracking, and changing all the IK 2.0 features to off, nothing fixes it. I dont want to be stuck doing the hand open gesture while i play the game. The whole point of the resting pose is for when I am not using any buttons.",
